7479 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157479 #edb/ref 1045 "The Distributive Laws" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157479 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186158130 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157479 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049989 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157479 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "d37ded1f-465b-5cac-8210-38b0f2560e8e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158099 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158107 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158099 #edb/ref 1061 26061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158099 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c82bb8aa-643d-5e50-a35d-e9ff0334ef10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158099 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158100 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158100 #edb/ref 1061 26062 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158100 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ee860d46-f0f0-59b9-9a98-146afd430ae9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158100 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158107 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158107 #edb/ref 1061 26194 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158107 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6cd4b57c-f668-5ec7-be21-0bd6afcf4614" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158107 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157278 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158108 #edb/ref 1061 26195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158108 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0df7beb5-c114-51ca-8751-453f137e4362" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158108 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157279 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158130 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158130 #edb/ref 1061 26412 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158130 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "30df3b4d-7faa-590a-8e72-6045fda318f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158130 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186158481 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158481 #edb/ref 1064 "Just like we can distribute multiplication over addition, we can also distribute conjunctions over disjunctions (and vice versa).\n\n- We can distribute a conjunction over a disjunction, as follows: $$A \\land (B \\lor C) \\equiv (A \\land B) \\lor (A \\land C)$$\n- Likewise, we can distribute a disjunction over a conjunction, as follows: $$A \\lor (B \\land C) \\equiv (A \\lor B) \\land (A \\lor C)$$\n\nThe rules above are called the **distributive laws** for propositional logic. To prove that these laws hold, we can construct truth tables.\n\n- The following truth table shows that $A \\land (B \\lor C) \\equiv (A \\land B) \\lor (A \\land C){:}$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,C\\,$ | $\\, A \\land (B \\lor C) \\,$ | $\\, (A \\land B) \\lor (A \\land C) \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ |\n\n- The following truth table shows that $A \\lor (B \\land C) \\equiv (A \\lor B) \\land (A \\lor C){:}$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,C\\,$ | $\\, A \\lor (B \\land C) \\,$ | $\\, (A \\lor B) \\land (A \\lor C) \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158481 #edb/ref 1065 4343 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158481 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "d5455bd3-2038-5ab8-ac8b-2dd7ec1df636" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158481 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
